course: dictionary
lesson: 13251
title: Names and rare words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a name for a person or a place, and some are also an ordinary word. Gilbert is a name: it is a boy's or man's first name, or a family name (a surname). You can often spot a name by its capital letter. «Gilbert kicked the ball over the fence.» Gilbert is a person here, because a person kicks a ball.
explain: Context tells you what kind of name it is. «The Gilbert Islands are in the Pacific Ocean.» Here Gilbert names a place. The sentence talks about islands and an ocean, so the clues show it is a place, not a boy.
explain: Gilbert also has a rare meaning with a small g: an old unit for measuring magnetic force. «The scientist measured the magnet in gilberts.» Words about magnets or science are the clues here. When you see a small g in a science sentence, check the words around it.
explain: You will almost never meet the science meaning in everyday reading. If the sentence is about a person, a story or a place, Gilbert is a name. If you are unsure, read the words around it, then check a dictionary.
fact: Gilbert is a name: a boy's or man's first name, or a surname.
fact: Names like Gilbert start with a capital letter.
fact: In «Anne of Green Gables», a story from Canada, Gilbert is a boy.
fact: The Gilbert Islands are part of Kiribati, in the Pacific Ocean.
fact: A gilbert, with a small g, is a rare old unit for measuring magnetic force.
exercise: «Gilbert kicked the ball over the fence before lunch.» What kind of word is Gilbert here? | A colour | A place on a map | *A name for a person | A unit for measuring magnets
exercise: «The Gilbert Islands are in the Pacific Ocean.» What does Gilbert name here? | A boy in a school | *A group of islands | A magnetic force | A type of boat
exercise: «The scientist measured the force in gilberts.» What is a gilbert here? | A character in a famous story | *An old unit for measuring magnetic force | A Pacific island | A boy's first name
test: «Gilbert and his sister walked to school.» Which clue tells you Gilbert is a person? | It has seven letters | The sentence is short | It is in the middle of the sentence | *He walked with his sister, and a sister is a person
test: Which of these is an old unit used to measure magnetic force? | Litre | Metre | *Gilbert | Second
exam: Look at «Gilbert painted the fence blue.» Which clue tells you Gilbert is a name here? | It is at the end of the sentence | It is a unit of measurement | *It starts with a capital letter, and a person painted the fence | It is a long word
